  "title": "Vectors",
  "content": "<p>A <strong>vector</strong> has magnitude and direction. Written as \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) (bold), \\(\\underline{a}\\), or \\(\\binom{x}{y}\\).</p><p><strong>Adding vectors:</strong> \\(\\binom{a}{b} + \\binom{c}{d} = \\binom{a+c}{b+d}\\). Join them nose to tail.</p><p><strong>Scalar multiplication:</strong> \\(k\\binom{a}{b} = \\binom{ka}{kb}\\). Scales the vector.</p><p><strong>Magnitude:</strong> \\(|\\binom{a}{b}| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\\).</p><p><strong>Paths:</strong> To find \\(\\overrightarrow{AB}\\), go from A to B via known vectors. \\(\\overrightarrow{AB} = -\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a}\\) if A is at position \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and B at \\(\\mathbf{b}\\).</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>\\(\\mathbf{a} = \\binom{3}{-1}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\binom{-2}{4}\\). Find \\(2\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}\\).</strong></p><p>\\(2\\binom{3}{-1} + \\binom{-2}{4} = \\binom{6}{-2} + \\binom{-2}{4} = \\binom{4}{2}\\)</p>"
 },
